From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abue Ammar <14371506+abue-ammar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:57:49 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] Use Full Disk Access when uninstalling, and wait for the app
 to quit (#1624)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* Use Full Disk Access when uninstalling, and wait for the app to quit

The uninstall scan checked for Full Disk Access by opening only the per-user
TCC.db. macOS 27 has no per-user TCC.db, so the check always failed, and
every Containers, Group Containers and Cookies row stayed locked even with
the grant (#844). The scan now uses Permissions.hasFullDiskAccess(), the
check File Search uses, which also opens the system TCC.db.

With the grant, the scan also finds each app's recent-documents list
(com.apple.sharedfilelist/…ApplicationRecentDocuments/<id>.sfl3). macOS
refuses even the listing without Full Disk Access.

Before trashing, the coordinator sent quit and started at once. An app that
is still quitting writes its saved state and preferences again, behind the
trash. It now waits for that copy of the app to exit. If the app does not
exit within the grace period, nothing is moved and a notice says so.

Items under /Library and /usr/local/bin stay locked: removing them needs
an administrator password, which Tinycast never asks for.

* Fix uninstall quit checks and show Full Disk Access in Permissions

* Align the Full Disk Access row with the other permissions

The row now reads its status from the same helper as Accessibility, and its
button says "Grant Access…" like the others. The footer repeated the
subtitle, so it is gone with its string. The coordinator test waits on a
deadline instead of 100 one-millisecond sleeps, so a slow runner cannot fail it.
